Why Is Demand Increasing
• Rising global security threats — Increasing asymmetric warfare, regional conflicts and cross-border military tensions are encouraging governments to strengthen short-range air-defense capabilities.

• Proliferation of UAVs and low-altitude threats — The growing use of drones and other low-flying aerial platforms is increasing demand for portable systems capable of engaging these targets.

• Advances in seeker technology — Improved infrared imaging seekers, target discrimination and countermeasure resistance are supporting development of next-generation systems.

Defense Technology Watch: MANPADS Move Toward Networked and Counter-UAS Roles
The MANPADS market is evolving alongside broader changes in short-range air defense. Intel Market Research highlights growing integration of advanced infrared seekers, digital interfaces and network connectivity. Systems are increasingly being considered as components of layered air-defense architectures rather than standalone infantry weapons.

The report also identifies counter-UAS applications as an important emerging use case. Lightweight systems are being evaluated for engagement of smaller and slower aerial targets, while manufacturers continue developing seeker and software modifications. At the same time, international export controls, end-user certification requirements and post-shipment verification continue to influence international market participation.

